  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "In question 1, you showed that $2^{10}=1024$. Use long multiplication to find $2^{20}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1\\,048\\,576$\n\nMultiply $1024$ by itself using long multiplication.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^{20}&=2^{10}\\times2^{10}\\\\2^{20}&=1024\\times1024.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{array}{rrrrrrrr}& & & &1&0&2&4\\\\\\times& & & &1&0&2&4\\\\\\hline& & & &4&0&9&6\\\\& & &2&0&4&8&0\\\\& &0&0&0&0&0&0\\\\&1&0&2&4&0&0&0\\\\\\hline&1&0&4&8&5&7&6\\\\\\hline\\end{array}$$\nTherefore $2^{20}=1\\,048\\,576$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 75
  },
